From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Wed, 07 Oct 2026 10:39:43 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7915: fix use-after-free in mt7915_mac_sta_poll

The station poll takes a station off the poll list under
sta_poll_lock, drops the lock, and then reads and writes the station.
If the station is removed in that window, the driver removal callback
finds the entry already off the list and does not wait. mac80211 then
frees the station while the poll still uses it. The poll runs in NAPI
context without the device mutex. The RCU read lock does not help,
because mac80211 frees the station with no grace period after the
removal callback.

Hold sta_poll_lock from the moment the poll takes a station off the
list until it is done with that station, and release it before the
next station. The removal callback then waits for the poll. mt7915 is
an MMIO device, so the register access under the spinlock does not
sleep.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 mt7915/mac.c |    6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/mt7915/mac.c
+++ b/mt7915/mac.c
@@ -111,8 +111,11 @@ static void mt7915_mac_sta_poll(struct m
 		msta = list_first_entry(&sta_poll_list,
 					struct mt7915_sta, wcid.poll_list);
 		list_del_init(&msta->wcid.poll_list);
-		spin_unlock_bh(&dev->mt76.sta_poll_lock);
 
+		/* Keep the lock while msta is in use: mt7915_mac_sta_remove()
+		 * takes it, and mac80211 frees the station right after that
+		 * call, without a grace period.
+		 */
 		idx = msta->wcid.idx;
 
 		/* get signal strength of resp frames (CTS/BA/ACK) */
@@ -128,6 +131,7 @@ static void mt7915_mac_sta_poll(struct m
 			mt76_rx_signal(msta->vif->phy->mt76->antenna_mask, rssi);
 
 		ewma_avg_signal_add(&msta->avg_ack_signal, -msta->ack_signal);
+		spin_unlock_bh(&dev->mt76.sta_poll_lock);
 	}
 
 	rcu_read_unlock();
